## Changelog Entries

### Version 1.2.0 (Feb 21, 2025)

**Title**: "Enhanced Real-Time Insights & Dashboard Overhaul"

**Summary**: This release introduces major improvements to our real-time data tracking dashboard, along with an upgraded UI for smoother navigation. We've also added enhanced filtering options, smarter notifications, and key performance boosts to elevate your analytics experience.

**Feature List**:
- New visual dashboard layout with modular widgets
- Live data stream optimization for faster sync across sources
- Fixed timestamp syncing issue on custom reports

**Details**: The newly designed interface includes customizable widgets that let users tailor their analytics view. Real-time tracking has been optimized with latency reduced by 40% across major input channels.

---

### Version 1.1.3 (Jan 20, 2025)

**Title**: "Smart Alerts and Reporting Enhancements"

**Summary**: This update focuses on smarter alert systems, better scheduled reporting, and behind-the-scenes system stability upgrades.

**Feature List**:
- Custom alert logic based on data thresholds and anomalies
- Improved scheduled reports with flexible timing and formatting
- Fixed export issue in PDF reports for filtered dashboards

**Details**: Users can define custom logic for alerts — traffic spike, inventory dip, or campaign milestone. Schedule report exports daily, weekly, or on performance-based triggers.

---

### Version 1.1.0 (Dec 23, 2024)

**Title**: "Introducing Data Unification Engine"

**Summary**: We've rolled out the Data Unification Engine — a core system update that brings fragmented data sources together in real time.

**Feature List**:
- Launch of the Data Unification Engine for syncing across CRMs, IoT, and analytics tools
- Optimized backend for faster cross-platform performance
- Patched minor API timeout issues during peak traffic hours

**Details**: Seamlessly brings together inputs from Salesforce, HubSpot, Shopify, IoT feeds, and more into one synchronized stream. 25% reduction in load times across API-driven applications.

---

## Changelog Layout CSS

```css
.changelog-entry {
  display: flex;
  gap: 32px;
  padding: 48px 0;
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(125, 164, 255, 0.16);
}

.changelog-date {
  flex: 0 0 120px;
  font-size: 14px;
  color: #9ba9c4;
}

.changelog-version {
  background: rgba(1, 117, 255, 0.2);
  color: #0175ff;
  padding: 4px 8px;
  border-radius: 4px;
  font-size: 12px;
  font-weight: 600;
}

.changelog-content {
  flex: 1;
}

.changelog-title {
  font-family: "Inter Display";
  font-size: 24px;
  font-weight: 500;
  color: #fff;
}

.feature-list li {
  color: #ccc;
  margin: 8px 0;
}

.feature-list li::before {
  content: "•";
  color: #0175ff;
  margin-right: 8px;
}
```

---

## Animation
- Entry reveal: Staggered fade in up on scroll
